    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Arctic climate science",
    "problem": "Defining Arctic amplification as a ratio of Arctic-to-global temperature change is statistically problematic, as the ratio's uncertainty becomes difficult or impossible to bound when the global temperature change (the denominator) is close to zero, leading to potentially inflated and misleading results.",
    "method": "The authors demonstrate using Fieller\u2019s theorem to develop confidence intervals for the ratio estimator of Arctic amplification, thereby properly quantifying uncertainty, especially when the reference global temperature change is close to zero.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze the statistical difficulties and problems in quantifying uncertainty that arise when defining Arctic amplification as a ratio of Arctic temperature change to a global reference change, particularly when the global change is close to zero.",
